{
  "name": "claude-provider-switcher",
  "displayName": "Claude Provider Switcher",
  "description": "Switch the Claude Code extension between API providers/gateways (LiteLLM, DeepSeek, MiniMax, local models, native subscription) with a sidebar UI, menu, hotkeys, and a status bar indicator.",
  "version": "0.9.1",
  "publisher": "AlekseiLobanov",
  "license": "MIT",
  "icon": "icon.png",
  "repository": {
    "type": "git",
    "url": "https://github.com/lobacom/claude-provider-switcher.git"
  },
  "homepage": "https://github.com/lobacom/claude-provider-switcher#readme",
  "bugs": {
    "url": "https://github.com/lobacom/claude-provider-switcher/issues"
  },
  "galleryBanner": {
    "color": "#181825",
    "theme": "dark"
  },
  "engines": {
    "vscode": "^1.83.0"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "test": "node --test \"test/*.test.js\""
  },
  "categories": [
    "AI",
    "Other"
  ],
  "keywords": [
    "claude",
    "claude code",
    "anthropic",
    "provider",
    "switcher",
    "model switcher",
    "llm",
    "gateway",
    "litellm",
    "openrouter",
    "deepseek",
    "kimi",
    "moonshot",
    "minimax",
    "qwen",
    "glm",
    "zhipu",
    "xiaomi mimo",
    "ollama",
    "lm studio",
    "llama.cpp",
    "vllm",
    "local llm"
  ],
  "activationEvents": [
    "onStartupFinished"
  ],
  "main": "./src/extension.js",
  "bin": {
    "claude-providers": "./bin/claude-providers.js"
  },
  "contributes": {
    "viewsContainers": {
      "activitybar": [
        {
          "id": "claudeProviderSwitcher",
          "title": "%container.title%",
          "icon": "media/sidebar.svg"
        }
      ]
    },
    "views": {
      "claudeProviderSwitcher": [
        {
          "id": "claudeProviderSwitcher.view",
          "name": "%view.name%"
        },
        {
          "id": "claudeProviderSwitcher.codexView",
          "name": "%view.codexName%",
          "when": "claudeProviderSwitcher.codexDetected"
        }
      ]
    },
    "viewsWelcome": [
      {
        "view": "claudeProviderSwitcher.view",
        "contents": "%welcome%"
      },
      {
        "view": "claudeProviderSwitcher.codexView",
        "contents": "%welcome.codex%"
      }
    ],
    "configuration": {
      "title": "Claude Provider Switcher",
      "properties": {
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.language": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "auto",
            "en",
            "ru",
            "zh"
          ],
          "enumItemLabels": [
            "Auto (follow VS Code)",
            "English",
            "Русский",
            "中文"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Follow VS Code's display language, falling back to English.",
            "English.",
            "Russian / Русский.",
            "Chinese / 中文."
          ],
          "default": "auto",
          "order": 0,
          "markdownDescription": "Language for the extension's own UI — menus, notifications, the sidebar, the status bar and the custom-providers table. Switches live. **Note:** command titles in the Command Palette and these setting descriptions are localized by VS Code's own display language, not this setting."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.switchAction": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "switch",
            "switchAndReload"
          ],
          "enumItemLabels": [
            "Switch provider",
            "Switch provider & reload window"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Switch the provider, then remind you to restart the session (new chat / Reload Window).",
            "Switch the provider and immediately reload the window so the next Claude Code session starts against the new provider."
          ],
          "default": "switch",
          "order": 1,
          "markdownDescription": "What happens when you switch a provider via the sidebar click, hotkey, cycle or menu. `Switch provider` leaves the running session alone (it sees the old env until restarted). `Switch provider & reload window` restarts the window right away — any unsaved work must be saved first."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.profiles": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Provider profiles (no limit; hotkeys cover the first 10). Managed via the **Claude Providers** sidebar, or edited here. Selecting a profile writes its `env` to `#claudeCode.environmentVariables#`. **Do not commit real API keys.**",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Stable internal id; links the profile to its API key in SecretStorage. Managed automatically."
              },
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "color": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "hotkey": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "env": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Environment variables written to claudeCode.environmentVariables. The API key (ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN) is NOT stored here — it lives in SecretStorage.",
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.customProviders": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Extra providers added to the **Add provider** menu, on top of the ones bundled with the extension. Use this to add a provider that isn't in the built-in list. Each row pre-fills a new profile's Base URL and (optionally) the model mapping; the API key is still entered per-profile and kept in SecretStorage.\n\nFor a table editor, run **Claude Provider: Manage custom providers…** (or the *Add provider* menu → *Manage custom providers…*) instead of editing the raw JSON here.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "name": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Display name shown in the Add provider menu (e.g. \"My Gateway\")."
              },
              "baseUrl": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL for the provider's Anthropic-compatible endpoint (e.g. https://api.example.com/anthropic). Leave empty for a native-subscription-style entry."
              },
              "codexBaseUrl": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional: the provider's OpenAI Responses API endpoint (e.g. https://api.example.com/v1). When set, it also appears in the Codex view's Add menu. A row with only this (no baseUrl) is Codex-only."
              },
              "local": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "default": false,
                "description": "List this under \"Local servers\" instead of \"Anthropic-compatible providers\"."
              },
              "icon": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional logo: a PNG file name under media/providers/, or a VS Code codicon id (e.g. \"server\"). Defaults to the server codicon."
              },
              "opusModel": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional default model for the Opus tier (ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL)."
              },
              "sonnetModel": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional default model for the Sonnet tier (ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL)."
              },
              "haikuModel": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional default model for the Haiku tier (ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL)."
              }
            },
            "additionalProperties": false
          }
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.codexProfiles": {
          "type": "array",
          "default": [],
          "markdownDescription": "Codex provider profiles, managed via the **Codex** view in the Claude Providers sidebar (or `claude-providers`). Switching writes `model_provider` / `model` / `model_reasoning_effort` and a managed `[model_providers.*]` block into Codex's `~/.codex/config.toml` (or `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml`); the rest of that file is left untouched. API keys are NOT stored here — they live in SecretStorage.",
          "items": {
            "type": "object",
            "required": [
              "name"
            ],
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Stable internal id; links the profile to its API key in SecretStorage. Managed automatically."
              },
              "name": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "key": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Its name in config.toml ([model_providers.<key>]). Assigned on creation."
              },
              "color": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "codex": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "base_url": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "OpenAI Responses API endpoint (…/v1). Empty = Codex's built-in OpenAI provider (codex login)."
                  },
                  "model": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "reasoning_effort": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "enum": [
                      "minimal",
                      "low",
                      "medium",
                      "high",
                      "xhigh"
                    ]
                  },
                  "http_headers": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  },
                  "query_params": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "additionalProperties": {
                      "type": "string"
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              "hotkey": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Optional Ctrl+Shift+Alt+<n> shortcut."
              },
              "fallbackId": {
                "type": "string",
                "description": "Id of the Codex profile to switch to when this one is unreachable."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.showStatusBarItem": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Show the active-provider indicator in the status bar."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.showCodexStatusBarItem": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Show the active Codex provider in the status bar (once you have Codex profiles)."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.codexKeyStorage": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "file",
            "config"
          ],
          "default": "file",
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Each Codex API key lives in its own owner-only file (~/.claude-provider-switcher/codex-keys/<id>.key); config.toml only references it through `auth = { command }` (`cat`, or `cmd /c type` on Windows). Every profile keeps its key, so `codex --profile <key>` works for all of them.",
            "The active provider's key is written into config.toml as `experimental_bearer_token` (plain text). Only the active profile has a key there."
          ],
          "markdownDescription": "Where the Codex switcher puts API keys for Codex to read. Keys are always kept in VS Code SecretStorage as well."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.showUsageStats": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "Show usage statistics (how many times each provider was switched to, and how long it has been active) in the sidebar and status-bar tooltips. Reset them with the \"Reset usage statistics\" command."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.showTokenStats": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "Show per-provider token usage (today, the last 7 days and the last 30 days) in the tooltips, read from Claude Code's session transcripts under `~/.claude/projects` and attributed to whichever provider was active when each session started. Turning this off disables transcript reading entirely. Reset the counters with the \"Reset usage statistics\" command."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.writeClaudeSettings": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Also mirror the active provider into the Claude Code **CLI** config at `~/.claude/settings.json` (under its `env` key), so a `claude` run in a plain terminal — not just the VS Code extension — uses the same provider. Only the keys this extension manages (`ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, the model/timeout vars) are touched; everything else in that file is left as-is. **Note:** this writes the active provider's API key into `~/.claude/settings.json` in plain text."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.shareKeysWithTerminal": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "Share provider API keys with the `claude-providers` terminal app, so it can switch the Claude Code CLI to any profile without VS Code running. The keys are mirrored to `~/.claude-provider-switcher/keys.json` (owner-only permissions) and keys entered in the terminal app are picked up here. VS Code's SecretStorage can't be read by other programs, so without this the terminal app asks for each key itself. **Note:** the keys are stored in that file in plain text."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.showRestartHint": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "markdownDescription": "After switching, tint the status bar item and add a reminder that the Claude Code session must restart (new chat / Reload Window) for the change to take effect. Clears on window reload."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.applyPinnedOnOpen": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": true,
          "description": "When a workspace has a pinned provider, automatically switch to it on open. Pin a provider via the sidebar (right-click → Pin to this workspace) or the command palette."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.autoFallbackOnApply": {
          "type": "boolean",
          "default": false,
          "markdownDescription": "When switching providers, first probe the target and, if it's unreachable, automatically fall back to its configured fallback provider (set per profile via **Edit → Fallback provider**). Adds a short network check to every switch. When off, use the **Switch with fallback** command for on-demand failover."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.healthCheck": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
            "manual",
            "periodic"
          ],
          "enumDescriptions": [
            "Only check reachability when you run the Check provider health command (default).",
            "Check all providers automatically on a timer (see healthCheckIntervalMinutes)."
          ],
          "default": "manual",
          "markdownDescription": "How the 🟢/🔴 reachability indicator is refreshed. The check uses `GET /v1/models`, which runs **no inference and costs no tokens**, so `periodic` is safe to leave on."
        },
        "claudeProviderSwitcher.healthCheckIntervalMinutes": {
          "type": "number",
          "minimum": 1,
          "default": 5,
          "markdownDescription": "How often (in minutes) to refresh provider health when `#claudeProviderSwitcher.healthCheck#` is `periodic`."
        }
      }
    },
